/**
	The rate of the voice (how fast it speaks), from -10 (slowest) to 10 (fastest), with 0 being the default.
	float tts_voice::rate;
	## Remarks:
		Values outside the range are clamped to it. Until it is assigned, it reports the rate the engine starts with, which may not be 0; see rate_set for what that is on each platform. With Speech Dispatcher on Linux, which uses its own configuration, it reports 0 until assigned, and assigning it doesn't change the speech. This is the property form of set_rate and get_rate.
*/

// Example:
void main() {
	tts_voice v;
	v.rate = 4;
	v.speak_wait("This is spoken faster than usual, at a rate of " + v.rate + ".");
}
